ree public exhibitions in Duke Hall","notes":"Visit with a small group during academic-year hours, choose one work each to discuss, and contact gallery staff ahead for groups larger than 35.","short_summary":"Use a rotating contemporary-art exhibition as the starting point for an informal group conversation.","evidence_claim":"The gallery’s official visitor page states that its exhibitions are always free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/dukehallgallery/visit.shtml","source_title":"About Duke Hall Gallery of Fine Art - JMU","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Public access during exhibitions. Academic-year hours are Tuesday through Saturday, 11 a.m.–5 p.m.; the gallery is closed in summer. Verify the current exhibition calendar.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-madison-art-collection-visit","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Madison Art Collection","title":"Browse the Madison Art Collection","subtitle":"A ticketless art stop on West Grace Street","notes":"Drop in with classmates during public hours, compare favorite pieces, or ask staff in advance whether a guided group tour can be arranged.","short_summary":"Spend an afternoon examining collection displays without buying admission or reserving a ticket.","evidence_claim":"The Madison Art Collection says it is free and open to all visitors and that its exhibitions are never ticketed, including group visits.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/madisonart/faq.shtml","source_title":"Madison Art: Frequently Asked Questions - JMU","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open to the public Tuesday through Friday, noon–4 p.m. Group visits do not require advance notice, although tours depend on staff availability.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-furious-flower-broadside-gallery-visit","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Furious Flower Broadside Gallery","title":"Read Poetry Through Visual Art","subtitle":"Free rotating broadside exhibitions at JMU","notes":"Bring a friend, read the displayed poems aloud or silently, and compare how each broadside’s visual design changes your response to the words.","short_summary":"Explore the meeting point of poetry and visual art through signed and limited-edition broadsides.","evidence_claim":"JMU’s Furious Flower Poetry Center states that the Broadside Gallery is free and open to the public and rotates exhibits about every other month.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/furiousflower/broadside-gallery/bring-your-class-to-visit.shtml","source_title":"Class Visits to the Furious Flower Broadside Gallery - JMU","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-05-22","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free public access; independent and class visits are welcomed. Contact the Poetry Center to confirm the current location, exhibit, and available visiting hours.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-community-seed-library-swap","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"JMU Community Seed Library","title":"Swap Seeds at the Community Seed Library","subtitle":"A self-service sharing activity with no library card needed","notes":"Browse the seed drawers together, take only what you can grow, and return labeled seeds later so the shared collection continues serving the community.","short_summary":"Plan a garden project with friends using JMU Libraries’ community seed-sharing collection.","evidence_claim":"JMU Libraries identifies the Community Seed Library as a self-service seed-sharing library available to everyone with no library card necessary.","source_url":"https://www.lib.jmu.edu/visitors/","source_title":"Services for Visitors and Alumni - JMU Libraries","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Available to all visitors during the host library’s operating hours; no library card is required. Check current library locations and hours before going.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-counseling-center-oasis-reset","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"The Oasis","title":"Take a Quiet Reset in the Oasis","subtitle":"A free student relaxation space in the Counseling Center","notes":"Bring your JACard, check in at the Counseling Center front desk, and share a quiet decompression break while respecting the room’s restorative purpose.","short_summary":"Pause together between classes in a student self-care room equipped with relaxation resources.","evidence_claim":"JMU’s Counseling Center says the Oasis is free for students to use after checking in with a JACard and notes that it includes massage chairs.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/news/counselingctr/2023/04-august_17_fall_semester_wellness_resources.shtml","source_title":"Counseling Center: Campus Wellness Resources - JMU","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-04-09","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current JMU students only. Check in with a JACard at the Counseling Center front desk in Student Success Center, third floor, Suite 3100.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-counseling-center-studio-create","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"The Studio","title":"Make Art Together in the Studio","subtitle":"Free student art supplies for a casual creative break","notes":"Check in with your JACard, pick a simple project everyone can try, and return shared supplies neatly when your low-pressure art session ends.","short_summary":"Gather for an informal creative session using the Counseling Center’s provided art materials.","evidence_claim":"JMU’s Counseling Center states that the Studio supplies art materials and is free for students to use after checking in with a JACard.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/news/counselingctr/2023/04-august_17_fall_semester_wellness_resources.shtml","source_title":"Counseling Center: Campus Wellness Resources - JMU","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-04-09","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current JMU students only. Check in with a JACard at the Counseling Center front desk in Student Success Center, third floor, Suite 3100.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-university-park-pickup-game","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"University Park","title":"Start a Pick-Up Game at University Park","subtitle":"Student courts, fields, and equipment without an extra fee","notes":"Swipe in with your JACard, choose pickleball, tennis, basketball, or another available activity, and check out shared equipment if your group needs it.","short_summary":"Turn an open court or field into a spontaneous game using equipment included for eligible members.","evidence_claim":"JMU says students have UREC membership, may play pick-up sports at University Park during operating hours, and can check out equipment at no extra cost.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/recreation/visit/guide.shtml","source_title":"University Recreation (UREC) Guide - JMU","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-05-14","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current JMU students and other eligible UREC members must swipe a JACard or use the UREC app. Facility access and equipment checkout are included; verify operating hours.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
